brainIMATE bundles the following libraries. Each keeps its own license; the texts are in
node_modules/<package>/LICENSE after an install. Versions are the ones this repository
installs from package.json, checked against the installed packages.

immer 11.1.21: undo and redo as patches of the document
MIT
https://github.com/immerjs/immer

bezier-js 6.1.4: curve math, nearest points, lengths and bounds
MIT
https://github.com/Pomax/bezierjs

fit-curve 0.2.0: turns the points of a pencil line into smooth curves
MIT
https://github.com/soswow/fit-curve

perfect-freehand 1.2.3: the outline of brush and eraser strokes, from the points and the pen pressure
MIT
https://github.com/steveruizok/perfect-freehand

bezier-easing 3.2.0: the ease curves of tweens
MIT
https://github.com/gre/bezier-easing

gifenc 1.0.3: GIF export
MIT
https://github.com/mattdesl/gifenc

mediabunny 1.61.3: WebM and MP4 export
MPL-2.0
https://github.com/Vanilagy/mediabunny
It brings in @types/dom-webcodecs and @types/dom-mediacapture-transform, types only, MIT.

fflate 0.8.3: compressed project files and the zip of an image sequence
MIT
https://github.com/101arrowz/fflate

idb-keyval 6.3.0: the autosave and the recent files in IndexedDB
Apache-2.0
https://github.com/jakearchibald/idb-keyval

browser-fs-access 0.38.0: the open and save dialogs, with a download where there is none
Apache-2.0
https://github.com/GoogleChromeLabs/browser-fs-access

tinykeys 4.0.1: the keyboard shortcuts
MIT
https://github.com/jamiebuilds/tinykeys

paper 0.12.18: boolean operations on paths (unite, subtract, intersect, exclude, divide), loaded only when one runs
MIT
https://github.com/paperjs/paper.js

Two more are build tools rather than runtime dependencies, but what they produce ends up in
the site, so they belong here too:

svelte 5 and @sveltejs/kit 2: the framework, and the runtime it compiles into every
component. Both float on a caret range, so the installed version is whatever the lockfile
last resolved
MIT
https://github.com/sveltejs/svelte

tailwindcss 4: the reset the theme is built on, compiled into app.css
MIT
https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss

Fonts are loaded at runtime from Google Fonts and are not redistributed here:
Instrument Serif, JetBrains Mono and Inter, all under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
